         <div type="letter">

 
<div type="mainBody">
<p>Dear <name type="person" key="weav76">Miss Weaver</name>: If anything appears tomorrow in <hi rend="underline">The</hi> <hi rend="underline">Observer</hi> about <rs type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">the book</rs> may I ask you to send a copy at once to:
        	<p>
                            <name type="person" key="fran78">Signor <seg xml:id="seg1" type="note-anchor">Alessandro Francini</seg>
                        </name>
                            <lb/>
        	Scala Pauliana 335<lb/>
        	
                            <name type="geo" key="ID_MISSING">Pendice di Scorcola</name>
                            <lb/>
        	
                            <name type="geo" key="G_ITA_TRIE">Trieste</name>
            </p>
He is giving a lecture on me there next Wednesday and I want him to have as many notices as possible.</p>
<closer>
<salute>With kind regards</salute>
                    	<signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
</closer>
</div>
</div>

<div type="notes">

<note xml:id="note1" target="#seg1" type="commentary">Alessandro Francini Bruni gave a lecture in Trieste on 22 February 1922, later published as <hi rend="italic">Joyce intimo spogliato in piazza (un’indiavolata caricatura dello scrittore irlandese)</hi>, Trieste: La Editoriale Libraria, 1922. An English translation was published in <hi rend="italic">James Joyce Quarterly</hi>, vol. 14, no. 2 (Winter 1977): 127-59.</note>

</div>


